claim.claim-text:
a) a front section, a central section and a rear section located along the longitudinal axis;
b) a backsheet having a garment facing surface;
c) a first pattern of fastening adhesive applied to the central section of the garment facing surface of the backsheet, the first pattern of adhesive comprising:

i) a first plurality of stripes extending substantially parallel to the transverse axis on a first side of the central longitudinal axis;
ii) a second plurality of stripes extending substantially parallel to the transverse axis on a second side of the central longitudinal axis; and
iii) a first gap between the first plurality of stripes and the second plurality of stripes, wherein the first gap extends over the central longitudinal axis.

i) a third plurality of stripes extending substantially parallel to the transverse axis on said first side of the central longitudinal axis;
ii) a fourth plurality of stripes extending substantially parallel to the transverse axis on said second side of the central longitudinal axis; and
iii) a second gap between the third plurality of stripes and the fourth plurality of stripes, wherein the gap extends over the central longitudinal axis.

i) a fifth plurality of stripes extending substantially parallel to the transverse axis on said first side of the longitudinal axis;
ii) a sixth plurality of stripes extending substantially parallel to the transverse axis on said second side of the longitudinal axis;
iii) a third gap provided between the fifth plurality of stripes and the sixth plurality of stripes, wherein the third gap extends over the longitudinal axis.
